-**FACT-REPO-ARCH-022** — Agent-worktree state comes from the Rust binary `agentwt` (`cmd/agentwt`, built to `bin/agentwt`, installed as `~/go/bin/smine-agentwt`): one JSON document per repo (`agentwt status --format json -C <repo>`, schema 1, committed at `cmd/agentwt/schema/status-v1.json`) carrying rows, base resolution, ahead/behind, one `containment` per row, sessions, merge order and per-phase timings. Everything is computed in process with gix in object-memory mode — inventory from refs and `.git/worktrees`, containment from an ancestor test, per own commit a no-op re-apply, replay (pick trailer, or the same author, author time and subject committed no earlier — conflict-resolved picks count) or patch-id twin among the candidate's commits after the branch's fork points, and a net check (merging the tip adds nothing); no worktrunk, no probe worktrees, no `git cherry` (worktrunk was measured against the gix inventory on 2026-09-25 and dropped: its one unique output duplicated the gix containment, see `plans/2026-09-25-rust-worktree-binary-wip-0abee699/verification/measurement.md`). `containment` names ONE branch in preference order base → default → any other candidate (`rank`), with `reason` `ancestor`, `all_commits_placed` or `merge_adds_nothing`; `null` means no single branch holds all of it, and `unpicked_commits` then lists the own commits no candidate holds. The base is the reflog's creation line unless a later rebase, reset or `branch -f` moved the branch onto another candidate (`reanchored`); a worktree mid-rebase or mid-bisect stays attached to its branch, and any operation in progress blocks `remove`. `cmd/agentwt/tests/scenarios/history.rs` is the history-shape catalog (rebase, pick, merge, base, worktree families) every containment change is checked against. The binary is a read-only overview plus one mutating command, `remove` (safety-gated, exit 3 on refusal); merge, cherry-pick and sync are deliberately absent. The shell scripts under `cmd/worktrees/` that did this (`print_agent_worktrees_status.sh`, `_lib/verdict.sh`, `merge_worktree.sh`, `cherry_pick_worktree.sh`, `sync_worktrees.sh`, `remove_agent_worktrees.sh`) and the `~/.claude/agents/tools` copy are gone; the config server decodes the JSON (`internal/repos/status.go`) and `/close` and the railroad cleanup call `smine-agentwt remove --delete-branch`. Entry points: `make rust-build`, `make rust-test`, `make rust-lint`, `make rust-load REPO=<clone> OLD=<checkout>`; the crate needs a rustup toolchain (`rust-version` 1.88 floor) that `make build` requires.
